osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2025-13465\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2025-13465](https://osv.dev/CVE-2025-13465)**.\n\n## [GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg](https://osv.dev/GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e The `_.unset`, `_.omit`, and `_.pullAt` functions are vulnerable to prototype pollution. An attacker can pass crafted paths which cause Lodash to delete methods from global prototypes.\n\u003e \n\u003e The issue permits deletion of properties but does not allow overwriting their original behavior.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e \n\u003e The issue is patched from 4.17.23 to 4.18.0 depending on the package: `lodash`, `lodash-es`, and `lodash-amd` in 4.17.23, and the standalone `lodash.unset` and `lodash.omit` packages in 4.18.0.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e \n\u003e None. Upgrade to the patched version.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/src/app/package-lock.json | lodash | 4.17.15 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg | lodash.unset | 4.18.0 |\n| GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg | lodash | 4.17.23 |\n| GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg | lodash-amd | 4.17.23 |\n| GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg | lodash-es | 4.17.23 |\n| GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg | lodash.omit | 4.18.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/src/app/osv-